    "Suffixes ic/ical, ist, eme, and the noun sense of y ('subject or science of') come from the Greek-form matrix suffix box (p.25) and are catalogued with frequency_rank=null; -ent (continent, pertinent) and -ual (factual, folded into able/ible's spellings) are irregular suffix spellings needed to segment 2 Word Key words that are not listed on any suffix chart.",
    "id 'y' (top-10 chart, 'marked by', adjective, e.g. rainy/sandy) and id 'y2' (Greek matrix suffix, 'subject or science of', e.g. biology/geography) share the surface spelling 'y'. No matrix uses a bare -y suffix in the adjective sense, so 'y' has an empty examples[] while 'y2' carries the real Greek-matrix examples."
